        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "07121830-33d3-5370-b8ad-970104fbf9ea",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Reginald Engelbach\n- Places: Cairo, Harageh, Egypt\n- Organizations: Egyptian Museum of Cairo\n- Roles: Egyptologist, engineer\n- Projects: excavation of the Harageh cemeteries, museum artifact register\n\nFacts:\n- Reginald Engelbach was born on July 9, 1888, and was an English Egyptologist and engineer.\n- In 1913, Reginald Engelbach excavated the cemeteries at Harageh.\n- Reginald Engelbach is mainly known for his work at the Egyptian Museum of Cairo, especially compiling a register of the museum's artifacts.\n- Cairo is the capital and largest city of Egypt.\n- Reginald Engelbach died on February 26, 1946.",
